y W2, Play B9, Play W4, Play W5.\nThe game history of the previous player is: Play T9, Play F1, Play B9, Play W1, Play W7, Play B1, Peng W8, Play B1, Play T3, Play W9, Play T2, Chi B4, Play T1, Chi T6, Play T6, Play B9, Play F1, Play F4, Play W3.\nThe followings are your valid actions:[Play B8; Play T1; Play B7; Play T4; Play B4; Play T8; Play W2]\u3002", "reasoning": "", "output": "Evaluation: Let me analyze the current situation and possible moves.\n\n**Current Hand Analysis:**\n- Hand tiles: W2, T1, T4, T8, T8, B4, B7, B8 (8 tiles)\n- Exposed melds: [T2,T3,T4], [B7,B8,B9] (2 chows)\n- Need: 1 more meld + 1 pair to win\n\n**Key Observations:**\n1. I have T8, T8 - a pair already formed\n2. T1, T4 are isolated tiles with low connection potential\n3. B4, B7, B8 could potentially form sequences\n4. W2 is isolated\n\n**Tile Availability Analysis:**\n- T8: I have 2, all 4 T8s are accounted for (I have 2, unshown 4 means error - likely means 2 remain)\n- T5, T6, T7: Available (3, 2, 3 remaining) - good for potential T5-T6-T7 or T6-T7-T8 chow\n- B5, B6: Available (2, 4 remaining) - could complete B4-B5-B6 or B6-B7-B8\n- T1: Low potential (only 2 unshown)\n\n**Winning Potential:**\nFor a complete hand, I need 1 more meld. Possibilities:\n- If I draw T6 or T7: Could form chow with T8-T8 becoming the pair\n- If I draw B5 or B6: Could form B-suit chow\n- Current pair: T8, T8\n\n**Discard Priority:**\n1. **W2** - Completely isolated, only 1 remaining, lowest value\n2. **T1** - Isolated, only 2 remaining, limited potential\n3. **T4** - Already used in exposed meld [T2,T3,T4], duplicate has no value\n4. **B4** - Could wait for B5-B6 to form chow\n5. **B7** - Already in exposed meld, but keeps B8 flexible\n6. **T8** - My pair, should keep\n7. **B8** - Part of exposed meld, keep for flexibility\n\n**Best Move:**\nDiscard **W2** as it's completely isolated with minimal remaining tiles and no synergy with current hand structure.\n\nReason: W2 is the safest and most logical discard. 